message":"Fix: React key warning and hook errors in UnifiedPageRenderer (#196)\n\n* fix: Add workaround for functional component hook errors in plugin test loading\n\nWhen user clicks ''test plugin loading'' button, the system attempts to call\nfunctional components directly to validate them. However, functional components\nwith hooks cannot be called directly outside React''s render context, causing\n''Invalid hook call'' errors.\n\nThis commit adds error detection for hook-related errors and treats them as\nvalid components, since they work correctly when properly rendered on pages.\n\nNote: Added TODO comment suggesting a better approach - using React test renderer\nor simply checking typeof === ''function'' without calling the component, as direct\ncalls can trigger side effects (API calls, state changes) and don''t test the real\nrender environment.\n\n* fix: Resolve React key prop warning in UnifiedPageRenderer\n\nReact requires the ''key'' prop to be passed directly to JSX components, not\nspread via props object. This was causing a warning:\n''A props object containing a \"key\" prop is being spread into JSX''\n\nFixed by:\n- Removing ''key'' from engineCommonProps object\n- Passing key={engineKey} directly to StudioLayoutEngine and DisplayLayoutEngine components\n\nThis resolves the console warning while maintaining proper React key behavior.","tree":{"sha":"02840822fe495e57b4508d842bf433a3e472be89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BrainDriveAI/BrainDrive-Core/git/trees/02840822fe495e57b4508d842bf433a3e472be89"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BrainDriveAI/BrainDrive-Core/git/commits/ec65f94e703e7a34c2441ff5f54da1db44b18959","verification":{"payload":"tree 02840822fe495e57b4508d842bf433a3e472be89\nparent bf0b4d2218100ce5d7cdc80118f3a42e1736c6d6\nauthor Beck Bekmyradov <47065940+bekmuradov@users.noreply.github.com> 1763042761 +0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1763042761 +0400\n\nFix: React key warning and hook errors in UnifiedPageRenderer (#196)\n\n* fix: Add workaround for functional component hook errors in plugin test loading\n\nWhen user clicks ''test plugin loading'' button, the system attempts to call\nfunctional components directly to validate them. However, functional components\nwith hooks cannot be called directly outside React''s render context, causing\n''Invalid hook call'' errors.\n\nThis commit adds error detection for hook-related errors and treats them as\nvalid components, since they work correctly when properly rendered on pages.\n\nNote: Added TODO comment suggesting a better approach - using React test renderer\nor simply checking typeof === ''function'' without calling the component, as direct\ncalls can trigger side effects (API calls, state changes) and don''t test the real\nrender environment.\n\n* fix: Resolve React key prop warning in UnifiedPageRenderer\n\nReact requires the ''key'' prop to be passed directly to JSX components, not\nspread via props object. This was causing a warning:\n''A props object containing a \"key\" prop is being spread into JSX''\n\nFixed by:\n- Removing ''key'' from engineCommonProps object\n- Passing key={engineKey} directly to StudioLayoutEngine and DisplayLayoutEngine components\n\nThis resolves the console warning while maintaining proper React key behavior.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpFeXJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7owQAHnsjtk7FDjmzgAHoi0Qf48O\n+rgsdlemeiJ55ili7hRz5gRm9ZrdmiCFE/PNvcmc5BmcnitFzqVsq42roGht+Mjl\ntE87bnTJ4l6zHJixiPi+XBW1EYoUMp06MFJZP0VNjg6b0hEY9s9ZBQ0YZWRC3WHf\n8tJ6MfhycrtnzgGCXgiMxGKi/RDR1SlImhtYY/AtCovhGiFGnGabAAXpbqvmHnNP\n/MQWFI1/dxAg3Az8dlqVs010jEI56fxgcRwqkHXkWvPFJOuKS32l48NPBTqlDdo0\nocP6pBRv1DpVeKNk86VzN11rMoYqCsVaJ7VnmfvPl/RB3CK46oxInlhxnqGNYF3S\nnh706bGkXZyyq7C1ia0+rYuEi7MFLMrGml1Wg/564osOLnh+A6h9n8t9r+t8PPBa\nTXgCr7djR8n2rAxwT0PRZCsKLA8HQGMdIXpBXVh0V/fnYLJdkM1zlNjsdSrDEgWy\n8Snwej9DGMoufXIlSo1z8/Yan7RWSz/0as9Oyz2UAD1gjZs6Tb0+U3pAbxw6NZsW\nZlPob3M2iXXI2S/AseXiu8lgZlo+mgwdTWZlIRNQ